==Nomenclature==
Sanke is borrowed from its Japanese name, {{Romanize|サンケゴイ|Sanke-goi}}, which is a reference to {{Romanize|三色|Sanke|tri-color|2}}, an alternative name for {{Wp|Koi#Varieties|Taishō Sanshoku}} variety of ornamental carp. In the Traditional Chinese, Simplified Chinese, Dutch, German, Canadian French, European French, Italian, Latin American Spanish, European Spanish, and Brazilian Portuguese versions of {{BotW|-}} and {{TotK|-}}, the translated names of Sanke Carp mean "tricolored carp".
{{Nomenclature}}

